     "finding": "Runs 3 and 4 establish a higher-pressure MgAl2O4 phase with CaTi2O4-type Cmcm structure. The authors construct its second-order Birch curve by fixing recovered V0, assuming K0'=4, and calculating K0 from the one usable compressed run-4 cell; run-2 CaTi2O4-type peaks were too weak and overlapped for a reliable cell volume."
    },
    "primary_data_check": {
     "status": "bundled",
     "audit_date": "2026-09-05",
     "dataset_identifiers": [
      "mgal2o4_cati2o4_funamori_1998_text_pv"
     ],
     "source_locations": [
      "Section 3.2, Tables 1-2"
     ],
     "finding": "The complete observations used by the source construction are bundled from printed pressure and lattice values. There is exactly one informative finite-pressure state; the source reports no supplementary materials, and the audit found no associated repository series."
    },
    "independent_refit": {
     "classification": "not_refittable",
     "method": "Analytical reproduction of the source's one-point construction: fixed recovered V0, K0'=4 implicit in BM2, and K0 equal to the normalized pressure of the rounded high-pressure lattice product.",
     "parameters": {
      "V0": 240.3,
      "K0": 206.40137542
     },
     "informative_finite_pressure_observations": 1,
     "degrees_of_freedom_for_residual_test": 0,
     "pressure_bracket_half_range_k0_gpa": 2.88897726,
     "published_curve_pressure_residual_gpa": -0.12504006,
     "finding": "The analytically reconstructed K0 differs from the published value by 0.40 GPa because the printed axes are rounded. Applying the same calculation to the ruby/Pt pressure bracket gives a 2.89 GPa half-range, reproducing the published +/-3 GPa uncertainty after rounding; there is no independent regression residual test."
    },
    "usage_recommendation": "not_recommended_for_quantitative_use"
   },
   "notes": "This record describes the CaTi2O4-type product established by runs 3 and 4. It is distinct from the lower-pressure CaFe2O4-type run-2 phase. It remains a production published record because the equation, coefficients, construction states, and provenance are complete, but it must not be presented as a multi-point fit."
  },
